{"base_rate":0.2722298221614227,"brier":0.11706880984952121,"bss":0.40910373011674905,"bss_hi":0.507892979680088,"bss_lo":0.2998505141111072,"country":"RO","deep":true,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split","Hourly verification","Frost and heat events","External benchmarks","Robustness checks","Recalibration test"],"ece":0.06477428180574558,"ess":362.65896444803286,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Bucharest</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Bucharest rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>82%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 731 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-30. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBUCURESTI FILARET, 1.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.41, ranked 32 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(11&ndash;62) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>350</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>87</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>82%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Bucharest</b> <span class=\"muted\">RO</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.41</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>11&ndash;62\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>731 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Bucharest &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Bucharest\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.36542857142857,377.84 83.2048,333.4666666666667 133.8455172413793,273.11379310344887 242.03083333333333,149.44444444444446 347.505625,52.125 407.35108433734945,18.0 407.35108433734945,31.15662650602411 347.505625,120.375 242.03083333333333,235.38888888888889 133.8455172413793,335.97701149425285 83.2048,372.29333333333335 59.36542857142857,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"282.90834473324213\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"282.90834473324213\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.36542857142857,364.32 83.2048,343.17333333333335 133.8455172413793,277.4022988505747 242.03083333333333,215.16666666666669 347.505625,109.0 407.35108433734945,83.7831325301205\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 350 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.36542857142857\" cy=\"364.32\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"83.2048\" cy=\"343.17333333333335\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 21%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 87 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"133.8455172413793\" cy=\"277.4022988505747\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 52%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"242.03083333333333\" cy=\"215.16666666666669\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"347.505625\" cy=\"109.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 82% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.35108433734945\" cy=\"83.7831325301205\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(27%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Bucharest the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.50) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (0.30).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>216</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.299</td><td class='num'>7.7%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>155</td><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'>0.366</td><td class='num'>5.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.455</td><td class='num'>7.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.498</td><td class='num'>7.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":44.43225,"lon":26.10626,"n":731,"n_cities":109,"name":"Bucharest","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0038571428571428576,"n":350,"obs":0.04857142857142857,"sig":true},{"hi":0.13,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.0712,"n":75,"obs":0.10666666666666667,"sig":false},{"hi":0.3500000000000017,"lo":0.13,"mean":0.21425287356321834,"n":87,"obs":0.28735632183908044,"sig":false},{"hi":0.7,"lo":0.3500000000000017,"mean":0.5198611111111111,"n":72,"obs":0.4583333333333333,"sig":false},{"hi":0.93,"lo":0.7,"mean":0.8178125,"n":64,"obs":0.75,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.93,"mean":0.9868674698795182,"n":83,"obs":0.8192771084337349,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.1,"rank":32,"rank_hi":62.0,"rank_lo":11.0,"reliability":0.00568688655138549,"resolution":0.08416561481312651,"slug":"bucharest","station":"BUCURESTI FILARET","timezone":"Europe/Bucharest"}